which needs review by Eyal the author,
to decide if these deployments can just be dropped:

turkey_metadata_2025july15.csv_version_1, the original had 22 rows.
turkey_metadata_2025july15.csv_version_2, by Eyal, had 17 rows dropping 5 problematic deployments.
turkey_metadata_2025july15.csv_version_3, by James, has 15 rows, dropping 2 following deployments:

	512201400 # no SSM

	512404801 # gets an error in code/R/IsrealTuna_99CI.R, this script only uses the 
	raw output file from the SSM, so the bug is presumably in the SSM itself.

================================================================================

The last script in IsraelTuna.m is calculate_time_in_Med_regions_IL.m which calculates stats.daysperhotspot:
I think the numbers in stats.daysperhotspot may be wrong.
But it might not matter, because it appears that stats.daysperhotspot is never used in the other scripts.
On the other hand, if you do use stats.daysperhotspot in your paper's
analysis, it may have incorrect results for the work previously done
on non-Turkey tuna.
Here is the error, which needs to be investigated further if stats.daysperhotspot is going to be used.
Note that it might run without error but erroneously if the number of TOPPIDs == number of Regions,
and no Region is empty.

>> calculate_time_in_Med_regions_IL
Error using ./
Arrays have incompatible sizes for this operation.

Error in calculate_time_in_Med_regions_IL (line 30)
stats.daysperhotspot.Alboran.prctdays.mean = mean((t./d.GroupCount)*100);
                                                    ^
 
>> size(t)

ans =

     0     1

>> size(d.GroupCount)

ans =

    13     1


